Z||000006||DjKid||08-15-2000||04:15 PM||||Well, I know what I'm gonna try.. I'm gonna swap out my Alt with the one off my bro's 87.. since he's got that engine out and not gonn ause it.. Alt's mine(so is the engine, going in my 88) We'll see if all is well afterwards.. lets hope! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>DjKid - 88 Coupe<BR>'Blue Knight"||||reg||1
Z||000007||Xtreme Fiero's||08-16-2000||11:56 PM||||before you go through the trouble of removing the alterantor you can test it while it is in the car.<P> Start the car as you would any other time & let it warm up then remove the ground from the battery, The car should NOT stumble or stall(if it does the alt. is bad) then look @ the voltmeter it should read about 16v (if not the alt. is going bad) when the battery is not hooked up. also rev up the car the Voltmeter should move like a small Tach, the voltmeter should never read below 14.4 volts or above 18.5.<P>You can also hook up a multimeter to the (+) side of the battery for a more accurate reading. also leave all the acc.'s and lights off for the test or you may damage a good alternator.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DjKid||08-17-2000||12:19 AM||||WEll, I did test it by taking the battery thingie off.. it died like really quick.. so I changed the alt's today.. YAY! All better.. Found out why my turn signal light on my dash was coming when I turned my lights on too... stupid me put the bulb in backwards  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> the Blue Knight is sweeter than sweet now.. beauty  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>DjKid - 88 Coupe<BR>'Blue Knight"||||reg||1
